complex_database.ml is `theorems := [ "ABELIAN_CHAIN_GROUP",ABELIAN_CHAIN_GROUP;
... ]`: every named theorem of the session make_complex.ml loads, for `search`
(help.ml), "for convenience where dynamic updating doesn't work".  The names
below are the OCaml names, in the OCaml order; each is paired with the Lean
theorem the OCaml identifier denotes at that point: the definition from the
last file in make_complex.ml's load order that binds it (as an OCaml binding
shadows earlier ones), or a core theorem.

Importing this module is `loadt "Multivariate/complex_database.ml"`: it loads
the files make_complex.ml loads before it (the imports below) and REPLACES
`Help.theorems` with this list, as the OCaml assignment does.  The list is
generated by ~/gxwork/cdb/gen_cdb.py (disclosed scaffolding); see that
script for how each name is resolved.
-/
